Time (after a long absence) to repost my VMS CPUs list. It was fairly up to
date to 1996, and I've recently put some of the newer Alphas in. However, I'd
welcome information about missing machines, and answers for any of the fields
with ?? in at present. This is a text listing out of Netscape, as once it's up
to date I'll make it available permanently as a web page in HTML.

------------------------- cut here ---------------------------------
VMS CPU Model Summary (12th May 1998)

The following table tries to summarises the whole publicly known Digital VAX
and Alpha model range by CPU type, divided into processor families, and then
by subtype, giving approximate chronological order. The information given
is:

   * The top byte of the SID in hex (containing the CPU type),
   * Processor subtype (XCPU or SYSTYPE).
   * Processor ID for VAXes.
   * Clock speed in MHz for AXPs.
   * Approximate speed, relative to a nominal VAX-11/780:
        o in VUPS for early machines,
        o in SPECmark89 (S) for later VAX workstations,
        o in SPECint92 & SPECfp92 for most AXPs,
        o scaled up SPECint95*38 & SPECfp95*42 for later Alphas,
        o scaled up SPECint_rate_base*5.2 & SPECfp_rate_base*5.0 for even
          later Alphas.
   * Main I/O bus type (U=UNIBUS, M=MASSBUS, C=CI, Q=QBUS, B=BI, D=DSSI,
     X=XMI, T=Turbochannel, F=Futurebus+, S=SCSI, E=EISA, P=PCI).
   * Model names.
   * Nickname.

Information is from publicly available sources such as DEC brochures and
press releases, together with the description of SYS$GETSYI in the VMS
documentation, and from $PRDEF, $VAXDEF, and $ALPHADEF in the system macro
library. This is supplemented with information from USENET group
comp.os.vms. Models thought to be current are marked by a leading `*'.

This list is not an official publication of Laser-Scan - ask DEC if you want
confirmed figures! In the fast changing world of computer hardware, its
probably out of date when written. However, please let me know of any
inaccuracies or omissions.

---
Paul Hardy (PGH), Product Manager (former Chief Programmer), Laser-Scan Ltd,
Science Park, Milton Rd, CAMBRIDGE, CB4 4FY, England. Email: PAUL@LSL.CO.UK,
Tel: (+44) (0)1223 420414; Fax: 420044, web: http://www.Laser-Scan.com
