Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec,comp.sys.vms,vmsnet.misc


I have a huge archive of binary data files mixing string, integer,
and floating point data that we we would like to read on other
platforms.  The integers and strings are not a problem.
The floating point is F_FLOAT format.  I would like a C routine
that could read these numbers and make them available on
other machines.
	XDR seems to be able to read the native and go to XDR,
but I don't think it can be told the file is F_FLOAT and then
convert to XDR.  CDF seems like it might be able to do this
type of thing, but haven't learned yet.
	One possible solution is to write the data to XDR
on the openVMS machine, and then can read the XDR format
anywhere else.  If anyone has written XDR binary on VMS,
pointers would be great.
	Any help much appreciated.  Thanks, D

