In article <6kf0vj$dlq$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>, brydon@physics.utexas.edu writes:
>	XDR seems to be able to read the native and go to XDR,
>but I don't think it can be told the file is F_FLOAT and then
>convert to XDR.

XDR as I know it is an API for translation between native and XDR formats.  You
need to convert to/from XDR on both ends of a socket opened between the reading
system and the system on which the data is resident.

FYI, I worked with a group who downloaded XDR from a Sun site, compiled it and
ran.  They claimed no modifications were needed.

